'' A BYVAL VAR-LENGTH STRING PARAMETER IS A POINTER to a descriptor the CALLER builds,
'' assigns into and deletes. Measured:
''
''     memset( &TMP$4$0, 0, 24 );
''     fb_StrAssign( &TMP$4$0, -1, &V$0, -1, 0 );
''     TAKEBYVALSTRING( &TMP$4$0 );
''     fb_StrDelete( &TMP$4$0 );
''
'' Passing the descriptor BY VALUE, which is what this did, gave the callee a second
'' owner of the caller's buffer: a callee that appends to its parameter reallocated it
'' and left the caller's descriptor dangling, and the caller then deleted the freed
'' pointer. It lowered and it verified. USTRING is the same shape through the U
'' entry points.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/byref-result.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
